{"body":"## Status\nOriginal Röver–Sapir Question 111 remains **unsolved after five substantive turns**. The complete independent source/proof review passes the scoped results. No full resolution or historical novelty is claimed.\n\nThe packet covers restricted wreath products, solvable PL images via credited Bieri–Strebel/BGK and Bleak inputs, simple-derived-factor subdirect products, and PL germ restrictions on torsion witnesses. The final finitely presented nilpotent examples are countermodels to an abstract proxy argument only: they are proved **not to embed in F**.\n\n## Frozen evidence\n- Preserves all 36 author files and 5 independent-review files\n- Author WIP ancestry: c1c399675089a7b7f9d9cb9320ee20ec89936198\n- Author manifest SHA-256: 0f21b2a22642240ab3d2bc1e285e7854875e9c27300c48e77f199cef3d254690\n- Review manifest SHA-256: a3418ac0f444baab1872824dd9850e1c74e5f5fb8ad6123d8e2fec872fe10ad9\n- 562,635 author and 110,736 independent bounded exact assertions pass\n- Standard-library Python only; `python verify_publication.py` verifies public hashes and both replays\n\nThe raw source PDFs/images remain local-only. The public replay explicitly omits those 20 historical local source checks, while retaining their original receipt. The source is OWR 26/2018, printed 1625, actually published April 12, 2019.\n\n## Scope\nFresh-main integration preserves author ancestry. The diff consists of 44 target artifacts and only this target's QUEUE status/turn cells, changed to unsolved 5/5. No merge or release.\n\n[Reviewed status and replay instructions](https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/blob/5b7bd8db9f34294d10862fed0f723055da864df6/problems/30003853_thompson_subgroup_abelianization/REVIEWED_STATUS.md)","headRefOid":"83862044e1bb334d582b2082bf8b63c6b0eee4c5","isDraft":true,"mergeCommit":null,"mergeStateStatus":"UNKNOWN","mergeable":"UNKNOWN","mergedAt":null,"state":"OPEN","url":"https://github.com/AlecKriebel/Math/pull/381"}
